        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 2,
        "titulo": "The typical English-speaker mistakes",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: the costliest mistakes: using the accusative with dative verbs, because English says \"help him\", \"thank him\", \"follow him\" (Ich helfe ihn / Ich danke dich instead of Ich helfe ihm / Ich danke dir); building «gefallen» like English \"like\" (Ich gefalle das Kleid instead of Das Kleid gefällt mir); and translating \"I'm cold\" word for word (Ich bin kalt instead of Mir ist kalt). STEP 2: read the table and say each correct sentence out loud before you look at the reason.",
        "erros": [
          {
            "errado": "Ich helfe ihn.",
            "certo": "Ich helfe ihm.",
            "motivo": "helfen takes the dative, even though English says \"help him\"."
          },
          {
            "errado": "Ich danke dich.",
            "certo": "Ich danke dir.",
            "motivo": "danken takes the dative: dir."
          },
          {
            "errado": "Ich gefalle das Kleid.",
            "certo": "Das Kleid gefällt mir.",
            "motivo": "gefallen = \"to please\": the thing is the subject, the person is dative."
          },
          {
            "errado": "Die Schuhe gefällt mir.",
            "certo": "Die Schuhe gefallen mir.",
            "motivo": "The verb agrees with the thing: plural gefallen."
          },
          {
            "errado": "Ich bin kalt.",
            "certo": "Mir ist kalt.",
            "motivo": "Feelings: dative + ist. \"Ich bin kalt\" means \"I'm a cold person\"."
          },
          {
            "errado": "Ich gratuliere dich zum Geburtstag.",
            "certo": "Ich gratuliere dir zum Geburtstag.",
            "motivo": "gratulieren takes the dative."
          }
        ],
